# Analog lock frequencies do not repeat

Operator rule (Ukrainian): **«одинакових частот між сесіями не буває»**.

- Each operator session has a **new** set of analog lock frequencies. Do not treat past MHz (3430, 3429, 5473, 5827, 1280, 1321, or any other) as “the usual bird”.
- Never assume last session’s MHz, IF winners (`channel_bw` / `deviation` / `sample_rate` / capture), or a `knob_sweep.csv` as the next bird.
- Ground truth picture is the other analog box OSD labelled **Rabbit**, not fpvscan’s last sweep.
- Sweep `--freq` is always whatever Rabbit / the console shows *this* session.

```text
# ❌ BAD — reuse last CSV / last MHz
python knob_sweep.py --freq 1321e6   # “worked yesterday”

# ✅ GOOD — this session’s Rabbit / console readout
python knob_sweep.py --freq <MHz from Rabbit>
```
